sequenceDiagram
    participant API as API Layer
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant Relay as Outbox Relay
    participant Kafka as Apache Kafka

    Note over API,DB: SYNCHRONOUS PATH — User waits for this
    API->>DB: Execute wCTE (Single Atomic Transaction)
    Note right of DB: WITH inserted_task AS (<br/>  INSERT INTO project_task ...<br/>  RETURNING *<br/>)<br/>INSERT INTO outbox_events<br/>SELECT 'task-events', id, payload<br/>FROM inserted_task
    DB-->>API: COMMIT — Both rows persisted or both rolled back
    API-->>API: Return HTTP 200 to Client (< 10ms)

    Note over DB,Kafka: ASYNCHRONOUS PATH — Runs independently
    DB-)Relay: pg_notify('outbox_event_notification')
    Relay->>DB: SELECT * FROM outbox_events\nFOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED LIMIT 100
    DB-->>Relay: Return locked batch
    Relay->>Kafka: ProduceRequest — Batch publish (partitioned by projectId)
    Kafka-->>Relay: ACK — All messages confirmed durable
    Relay->>DB: DELETE FROM outbox_events WHERE id IN (...)\n(Hard delete — keeps table near-zero size)

    Note over Relay,Kafka: Crash Safety: If crash before DELETE,\noutbox rows are re-fetched on next poll cycle
